---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const words = [
 ['der Beamer','die Beamer','projector'],['das Buch','die Bücher','book'],['der Computer','die Computer','computer'],['das Fenster','die Fenster','window'],['das Heft','die Hefte','exercise book'],['der Stift','die Stifte','pen'],['der Stuhl','die Stühle','chair'],['die Tafel','die Tafeln','board'],['der Tisch','die Tische','table'],['die Tür','die Türen','door'],['die Uhr','die Uhren','clock / watch'],['die Zahl','die Zahlen','number'],
];
const numbers = ['eins','zwei','drei','vier','fünf','sechs','sieben','acht','neun','zehn','elf','zwölf','dreizehn','vierzehn','fünfzehn','sechzehn','siebzehn','achtzehn','neunzehn','zwanzig'];
const questions = [
 {prompt:'7 = ___',options:['sechs','sieben','siebzehn'],answer:'sieben',why:'Seven is sieben. Seventeen is siebzehn.'},
 {prompt:'12 = ___',options:['zwei','zwölf','zwanzig'],answer:'zwölf',why:'Twelve is zwölf.'},
 {prompt:'16 = ___',options:['sechzehn','sechszehn','sechzig'],answer:'sechzehn',why:'Sixteen is sechzehn, without the final s of sechs.'},
 {prompt:'20 = ___',options:['zwölf','zehn','zwanzig'],answer:'zwanzig',why:'Twenty is zwanzig.'},
 {prompt:'Was ist das? Das ist ___ Buch.',options:['ein','eine'],answer:'ein',why:'Buch is neuter: das Buch, ein Buch.'},
 {prompt:'Wie viele Stühle ___ das Klassenzimmer?',options:['habe','hast','hat'],answer:'hat',why:'Das Klassenzimmer takes the same verb form as es: hat.'},
 {prompt:'ein Heft → zwei ___',options:['Heft','Hefte','Heften'],answer:'Hefte',why:'The plural is die Hefte.'},
 {prompt:'ein Fenster → zwei ___',options:['Fenster','Fenstern','Fensters'],answer:'Fenster',why:'Fenster does not change in the plural: die Fenster.'},
];
---
<Base title="Lesson 2: zählen 1 — numbers and everyday objects" description="Practise German numbers 1–20, everyday objects, articles and the verb haben with guided learning activities.">
<div class="lesson-two">
 <header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <a class="back" href="/resources/german-async#e1">← Back to your learning path</a>
  <p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 02 · MAIN LESSON</p>
  <h1>Small numbers.<br /><em>Everyday discoveries.</em></h1>
  <p class="intro">Count to twenty, name the things around you, and say what you have.</p>
  <p class="context">Start here for <span lang="de">Lektion 2: zählen 1</span>. Work through the four steps below, then continue to the <a href="/resources/german-lesson-2">extension practice</a>.</p>
  <nav aria-label="Lesson steps"><a href="#watch">01 Watch</a><a href="#words">02 Review</a><a href="#practice">03 Practise</a><a href="#speak">04 Speak</a></nav>
 </div></header>
 <div class="wrap lesson-body">
 <section id="watch" aria-labelledby="watch-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 / WATCH &amp; LISTEN</p><h2 id="watch-title">Start with the video.</h2><p>Listen for the numbers. Watch once, then replay and say the numbers aloud. Use the number list below to check the spelling.</p>
 <div class="video"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/qIGBan6NIl0?si=zIDIK9SJ2zCrztFX" title="Lesson 2: German numbers 1–20" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
 <p class="small">Internet required. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qIGBan6NIl0">Watch on YouTube</a> if the player does not load.</p></section>
 <section id="words" aria-labelledby="words-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / BUILD YOUR VOCABULARY</p><h2 id="words-title">The things around you.</h2><p>Say each noun with its article, then say its plural. Learn the three together.</p>
 <ul class="word-grid">{words.map(([noun,plural,english])=><li><span>{english}</span><h3 lang="de">{noun}</h3><p lang="de">{plural}</p></li>)}</ul>
 <h3 class="subheading">Count from 1 to 20.</h3><ol class="numbers">{numbers.map((word,i)=><li><span>{i+1}</span><strong lang="de">{word}</strong></li>)}</ol>
 <p class="tip">Try saying this practice phone number one digit at a time: <strong>6 – 5 – 1 – 2 – 7 – 2 – 9</strong>. Use an invented number when practising with others.</p></section>
 <section id="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / UNDERSTAND &amp; PRACTISE</p><h2 id="practice-title">Put the pieces together.</h2>
 <div class="grammar-grid"><article><h3 lang="de">der, die, das</h3><p>In the nominative (the dictionary form), the article matches the noun’s gender. Learn it with the noun.</p><ul><li>Masculine: <strong lang="de">der Tisch · ein Tisch</strong></li><li>Feminine: <strong lang="de">die Tür · eine Tür</strong></li><li>Neuter: <strong lang="de">das Buch · ein Buch</strong></li><li>Plural: <strong lang="de">die Bücher</strong> (no plural of <em>ein</em>)</li></ul></article>
 <article><h3 lang="de">haben · to have</h3><p>Choose the form that matches the person.</p><ul lang="de"><li><strong>ich habe</strong> · I have</li><li><strong>du hast</strong> · you have (informal)</li><li><strong>er / sie / es hat</strong> · he / she / it has</li><li><strong>wir / sie / Sie haben</strong> · we / they / you (formal) have</li><li><strong>ihr habt</strong> · you (plural, informal) have</li></ul></article></div>
 <p class="tip">After <strong lang="de">haben</strong>, the thing you have is a direct object. Masculine <strong lang="de">ein</strong> becomes <strong lang="de">einen</strong>: <span lang="de">Ich habe einen Stift.</span> Feminine <strong>eine</strong> and neuter <strong>ein</strong> stay the same here.</p>
 <p>Choose one answer for each sentence, then check your work. You can change your answers and try again.</p>
 <form id="lesson-quiz">{questions.map((q,i)=><fieldset data-answer={q.answer} data-explanation={q.why}><legend><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span> <span lang="de">{q.prompt}</span></legend><div class="choices">{q.options.map(option=><label><input type="radio" name={`q${i}`} value={option}/><span lang="de">{option}</span></label>)}</div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>)}<div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p id="quiz-score" role="status"></p></form>
 <noscript><p>Interactive checking needs JavaScript. Answer key: {questions.map((q,i)=>`${i+1}. ${q.answer}`).join(' · ')}.</p></noscript>
 </section>
 <section id="speak" aria-labelledby="speak-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SPEAK &amp; EXPLORE</p><h2 id="speak-title">What’s in the room?</h2><p>Read this model aloud. Then replace the objects and numbers with things around you.</p>
 <div class="grammar-grid"><article lang="de"><h3>Johannes &amp; Yasmin</h3><p><strong>Johannes:</strong> Finden Sie einen Stuhl.</p><p><strong>Yasmin:</strong> Da ist ein Stuhl.</p><p><strong>Johannes:</strong> Wie viele Stühle hat das Klassenzimmer?</p><p><strong>Yasmin:</strong> Das Klassenzimmer hat 16 Stühle.</p></article><article lang="de"><h3>Julia &amp; Max</h3><p><strong>Julia:</strong> Was ist das?</p><p><strong>Max:</strong> Das ist ein Tisch.</p><p><strong>Julia:</strong> Wie viele Tische hat das Klassenzimmer?</p><p><strong>Max:</strong> Das Zimmer hat 8 Tische.</p></article></div>
 <h3 class="subheading">Your turn.</h3><ol class="speaking"><li>Point to an object and ask <span lang="de">“Was ist das?”</span> Answer with <span lang="de">“Das ist …”</span> and its article.</li><li>Ask <span lang="de">“Wie viele Bücher / Stifte / Hefte / Computer hast du?”</span> Count and answer using <span lang="de">“Ich habe …”</span>.</li><li>With a partner or group, take turns counting from 1 to 20. On your own, count aloud and repeat without looking.</li></ol>
 <h3 class="subheading">Culture: counting with your hands.</h3><p>Try counting on your fingers. Which finger do you start with? The source lesson invites you to explore counting gestures and greetings in German-speaking countries. Compare examples with your own habits, remembering that gestures and preferences vary between people and situations.</p>
 <a class="next" href="/resources/german-lesson-2">Next: extension practice →</a><p class="small">Review vocabulary, practise articles and <span lang="de">haben</span>, then write sentences about your own objects.</p></section>
 <aside class="source"><h2>Source &amp; adaptation</h2><p>Adapted from <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l2/">Grenzenlos Deutsch, Lektion 2: zählen 1</a>, supplied as a saved-page ZIP, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Numbers, vocabulary, model dialogue and learning tasks are drawn from the source. Explanations are condensed, cultural prompts are adapted, and eight new text-based questions replace the original embedded activities. The archive did not include the standalone audio files or all files required for the original exercises. The original lesson remains linked above for those materials. YouTube playback requires internet and remains subject to the video owner’s rights. This page has no offline-saving feature.</p><p>Original funding: National Endowment for the Humanities and the Mansergh-Stuessy Fund for College Innovation. Ramzunā Languages is not affiliated with the original authors.</p></aside>
 </div>
</div>
</Base>
<script>
const quiz = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#lesson-quiz');
quiz?.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();let score=0;const fields=quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLFieldSetElement>('fieldset');fields.forEach(field=>{const selected=field.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked');const correct=selected?.value===field.dataset.answer;if(correct)score++;const feedback=field.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.feedback')!;feedback.textContent=!selected?'Choose an answer first.':`${correct?'Correct.':'Not quite.'} ${field.dataset.explanation}`;field.dataset.result=!selected?'empty':correct?'correct':'incorrect';});document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent=`${score} of ${fields.length} correct. Review the feedback above and try again whenever you like.`;});
quiz?.addEventListener('reset',()=>{quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.feedback').forEach(el=>el.textContent='');quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('fieldset').forEach(el=>delete el.dataset.result);document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent='';});
</script>
<style>
